{
  "name": "hlc-format",
  "endpoint": "n/a",
  "description": "The HLC as it travels: physical unix milliseconds zero-padded to 15 digits, counter to 5, then the device id, which may itself contain colons. The padding is the point — the server compares the column as text, and that order has to be the domain order. Times beside them are UTC ISO 8601 with milliseconds.",
